<title>UK: GOLF-ELS REPLACES WOODS AS WORLD NUMBER ONE.</title>
<headline>GOLF-ELS REPLACES WOODS AS WORLD NUMBER ONE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ernie Els has become the first</p>
<p>South African to head the world golf rankings following his U.S.</p>
<p>Open and Buick Classic victories.</p>
<p>Els took over as number one in Monday's rankings from Tiger</p>
<p>Woods, who held the position for just one week.</p>
<p>The South African became the 10th player to lead since the</p>
<p>rankings began in 1986.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>  1. Ernie Els (South Africa)	 9.95 points average</p>
<p>  2. Tiger Woods			  9.68</p>
<p>  3. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)    9.61</p>
<p>  4. Greg Norman (Australia)	  9.51</p>
<p>  5. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	    9.24</p>
<p>  6. Tom Lehman			   8.96</p>
<p>  7. Steve Elkington (Australia)    8.74</p>
<p>  8. Masahiro Ozaki (Japan)	   8.11</p>
<p>  9. Mark O'Meara			 7.53</p>
<p> 10. Nick Faldo (Britain)	     7.07</p>
<p> 11. Phil Mickelson		     7.06</p>
<p> 12. Brad Faxon			   6.86</p>
<p> 13. Scott Hoch			   6.81</p>
<p> 14. Fred Couples			 6.79</p>
<p> 15. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)	 5.67</p>
<p> 16. Bernhard Langer (Germany)	5.57</p>
<p> 17. Ian Woosnam (Britain)	    5.44</p>
<p> 18. Davis Love III		     5.27</p>
<p> 19. Vijay Singh (Fiji)		 5.02</p>
<p> 20. Tom Watson			   4.97</p>
</text>
